  "family": "Agavaceae",
  "memo": "Cabbage palm is an evergreen tree native to New Zealand. It has a distinctive form, with multiple branches topped by dense rosettes of long, sword-shaped leaves. Once established, it tolerates heat, drought, poor soils, wind, salt spray, and frost, making it a popular ornamental and landscape plant. The species generally grows to less than 25 feet tall and produces large clusters of small, strongly scented white flowers. Despite its palm-like appearance, &lt;em&gt;C. australis&lt;/em&gt; is not a true palm but a member of the asparagus family, Asparagaceae.&nbsp;",
