  "california_native": 0,
  "ethnobotanical_info": "Cabbage tree was an important resource for Māori people of New Zealand. Its leaves were used to make baskets, sandals, and cordage, while the rootstock provided an important food source. The trees were also used as landmarks and markers of boundaries, a tradition that continues today through their deliberate planting in the landscape.",
